# A failure in dd::init(DD_RESTART_OR_UPGRADE) must abort the server cleanly
# with exit code 1. It must not crash inside VillageSQL's upgrade predicate.
#
# Guards the upgrade_needed assert found in the Percona Server 8.4.10 merge;
# burn-down entries innodb.autoinc_persist_debug and main.lowercase_fs_off.
#
# dd::init() runs SchemaManager::preinit(), and runs it even when
# restart_dictionary() has already failed. preinit_for_restart() then cannot
# read villagesql.properties, so it returns early without recording whether a
# VillageSQL upgrade is needed. The failure branch of init_server_components()
# -- added by Percona's PS-8257 -- calls
# dd::upgrade::no_server_upgrade_required(), which reaches
# SchemaManager::is_villagesql_upgrade_needed(). Asking that question before it
# had an answer aborted on an assert in a debug build, and dereferenced a null
# pointer in a release build, instead of returning.
#
# Covered upstream only incidentally, by two tests that assert on the exit code
# for unrelated reasons: innodb.autoinc_persist_debug (BUG#31763837, a DD
# truncate assert) and main.lowercase_fs_off, which reaches this path for real
# via a mismatched --lower_case_table_names but runs only on a case-sensitive
# filesystem. error_during_bootstrap returns from restart_dictionary() ten lines
# above that LCTN check, so this pins the same path on every platform.

--source include/have_debug.inc

--echo # Stop the server, then start it with a forced bootstrap failure.
--source include/kill_mysqld.inc

--echo # Expect a clean abort (exit 1), not a crash (exit 2).
--error 1
--exec $MYSQLD_CMD --debug=+d,error_during_bootstrap

--echo # The server still starts normally afterwards.
let $restart_parameters = "restart:";
--source include/start_mysqld.inc

SELECT 1 AS server_started;
